I've been playing Nethack for a week or two now. I'm spoiled rotten of
course, and I feel like I know a lot about the game, but having
knowledge and applying that knowledge are two different things.

That said I think I have a character who can go all the way, assuming
smart and careful play. I should point out that this is the first
character I've gotten through Sokoban.

Starting out I decided to stick to a single class. That way I could
hone in on a certain set of early game tactics. Moreover, I chose one
of the weaker classes (archeologist) to force myself to learn good
playing skills like thorough searching and careful pet management.

I made it easy on myself by rolling a lawful dwarf, so the mines are a
cakewalk assuming I can keep my pet in line. The protection racket is
pretty easy to run with this character, and that's how I started this
game. Got to Minetown at XL:1 with about 2000g, enough for a few
points of protection. My kitty cleared all the watchmen out for me,
and I went back to clear the earlier levels to beef up my XL and my
skill in pick-axe. Minetown spawned with lots of shops and Izchak had
a magic lamp for me. I managed to score some dwarven mithril and a
cloak of protection, and get a few decent intrinsics.

I decided to try my hand at Sokoban. Unfortunately my kitty met an
untimely end somewhere out of my sight, but I did manage to find a
longsword and dip for Excalibur. I enchanted what I could and headed
in. Sokoban started out poorly when some kobold used one of the
scrolls of earth as soon as I got inside, so I had to break a few
boulders, but my reward was twofold: amulet of reflection, and
knowledge. On the last floor I had a remarkably easy time clearing out
the zoo, which was my first indication that I wasn't a complete
weakling anymore.

(About this time I rubbed my lamp, which didn't give me a wish but did
give me a pet djinni. He lasted until I fell through a pit trap
somewhere around my quest, and when I went back up to get him he was
no longer tame. Oh well.)

Feeling pretty good I went to finish up the mines. I found a gray
stone on the bottom level and kicked it to see if it was load or luck.
It flew across the room and murdered a (friendly) gnome. That
demoralized me enough, but when I went to retrieve the stone I
couldn't find it anywhere. It just vanished. I figured one of the
other friendlies must have picked it up, so I murdered them all (and
felt horribly guilty about it). Strike two. Then, irritated that I
might have just lost my luckstone, I happened across another gray
stone in the next room. Picked it up without thinking, and of course
this one was a loadstone. Strike three! I was about to quit then and
there until I sat down and cooled off, looked at EVERYTHING I was
carrying, and came up with a solution. I had an identify scroll, a
magic marker, and one bottle of holy water. I couldn't remember if I'd
identified remove curse or not, but I gave it a shot, and bing! It
worked. I blessed the marker, wrote the scroll, and was free of my
dead weight. Even better, I eventually found my luckstone; it was just
laying under someone's corpse. Another lesson well-learned: you're not
out until you're out.

The floor below Sokoban had a co-aligned alter, and the floor below
that had a magic trap. I spent a while popping the trap and carting
the corpses it scored me upstairs (hoping to get back in Quetzacoatl's
good graces after murdering all those helpless gnomes and dwarves) and
eventually this got me Graswandir. The trap then expired, so I went
back to DL:1 thinking I could clear out a bunch of monsters and up my
weapon skill. I tore through a swarm of soldier ants, helpfully
supplying me with poison resistance.

Still no magic resistance, but there was nothing that could be done
about it. I continued descending until I hit my quest, which was
surprisingly easy. Took especial care to tiptoe around eels and mind
flayers as I went down through Medusa, solved my passtune and
slaughtered the castle army with the drawbridge. My wand scored me
five wishes: blessed scrolls of charging, grey dragon scale mail,
blessed scrolls of genocide (used one on L right away and am saving
the other for an emergency), blessed helm of brilliance, and a blessed
archon figurine.

Now I'm sitting on the cusp of Gehennom. I've got reflection and magic
resistance, the archon figurine in my pocket, and am twoweaponing with
Graswandir and a silver saber. I've got a bag of holding and a magic
whistle and a unihorn and a towel.

As far as I can see I have three major weaknesses right now: I lack
fire resistance (I have shock, cold, and disintegration though), I
don't have teleport control, and my AC is only -21. Is it time to
descend into Gehennom now? I have one scroll of charging left, which I
could use on my empty marker, which could then write me a bunch of
enchant armor scrolls, so that's how I might start out tomorrow.
Should I pre-emptively take out mind flayers, or save my genocide
scroll for an emergency? Or take out mimics to score more goodies as I
descend? Take out my archon now, or wait until I'm up against the big-
name demons? I feel confident and incredibly vulnerable at the same
time.

It's very exciting!


